                <div class="explainer-content">
                    <strong>How are threat actors connected to OpenClaw instances?</strong>
                    <p>We enrich each exposed instance's IP address through SecurityScorecard threat intelligence. When an IP has historical association with APT infrastructure, C2 servers, or known threat actor campaigns, that linkage is recorded. An instance "linked to Kimsuky" means the hosting infrastructure has been flagged in threat intel feeds as associated with that group's operations.</p>
                    <p style="margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;opacity:0.8"><strong>Date Disclaimer:</strong> The "Last Scanned" date shown represents when SecurityScorecard last observed this IP in threat intelligence feeds, not necessarily when the threat actor attribution was first established.</p>
