                    <h2>OSINT Collection Methodology</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="section-explainer">
                    <h4>Automated Discovery</h4>
                    <p>We use targeted Google dorks to discover exposed configurations, leaked credentials, and public discussions about OpenClaw deployments. All findings are validated before inclusion.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="dork-categories">
                    <div class="dork-cat"><span class="dork-cat-name">Credential Leaks</span><span class="dork-cat-desc">API keys, tokens, and secrets in public repositories</span></div>
                    <div class="dork-cat"><span class="dork-cat-name">Configuration Files</span><span class="dork-cat-desc">Exposed .env files, config.json, docker-compose</span></div>
                    <div class="dork-cat"><span class="dork-cat-name">Paste Sites</span><span class="dork-cat-desc">Pastebin, GitHub Gists with OpenClaw references</span></div>
                    <div class="dork-cat"><span class="dork-cat-name">Social Discussions</span><span class="dork-cat-desc">Reddit, Twitter, forums discussing security issues</span></div>
                    <div class="dork-cat"><span class="dork-cat-name">Error Messages</span><span class="dork-cat-desc">Publicly indexed stack traces and debug output</span></div>
                </div>
            </section>
