            <section class="research-section">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div class="section-icon strike-icon"><img src="/assets/strike_icon.png" alt="STRIKE" /></div>
                    <h2>ClawHub Skill Intelligence</h2>
                    <span class="section-badge danger">1-3+ objects/row</span>
                </div>
                <div class="section-explainer">
                    <h4>Collection: clawhub-skills &mdash; Powered by Clawdex (Koi Security)</h4>
                    <p>Each skill from ClawHub produces a STIX <code>tool</code> object. Malicious skills additionally generate <code>indicator</code> objects for each C2/payload URL and <code>relationship</code> SROs linking them. Verdicts and analysis powered by the Clawdex API.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-tw">
                    <table class="taxii-t">
                        <thead><tr><th>STIX Type</th><th>Category</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><span class="stix-tag">tool</span></td><td>SDO</td><td>Skill name, version, Clawdex verdict, summary. Custom extensions: <code>x_clawdex_verdict</code>, <code>x_clawdex_explanation</code>, <code>x_clawdex_attribution</code>. Labels: <code>malicious|benign|suspicious</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td><span class="stix-tag">indicator</span></td><td>SDO</td><td>For malicious skills: STIX pattern for each C2/payload URL from Clawdex analysis. Labels: <code>malicious-activity</code>, <code>c2-url</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td><span class="stix-tag">relationship</span></td><td>SRO</td><td><code>tool</code> &rarr; <code>indicates</code> &rarr; <code>indicator</code> linking malicious skills to their C2 infrastructure</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- AUTHENTICATION & USAGE -->
            <div class="section-group-header"><h3><span>Authentication & Usage</span></h3></div>

            <section class="research-section">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div class="section-icon strike-icon"><img src="/assets/strike_icon.png" alt="STRIKE" /></div>
                    <h2>Authentication Flow</h2>
                    <span class="section-badge">HTTP BASIC</span>
                </div>
                <div class="section-explainer">
                    <h4>API Key via HTTP Basic Auth</h4>
                    <p>All TAXII endpoints require authentication. Keys are issued by the STRIKE team and grant full access to all collections.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-tw">
                    <table class="taxii-t">
                        <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>1</td><td>Request a key</td><td>Contact <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#6f1c1b1d06040a2f1c0a0c1a1d061b161c0c001d0a0c0e1d0b410600"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="374443455e5c527744525442455e434e445458455254564553195e58">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> to request a TAXII API key</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>2</td><td>Authenticate</td><td>Use HTTP Basic Auth with username <code>taxii</code> and your API key as the password</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>3</td><td>Key hashing</td><td>Keys are SHA-256 hashed server-side. The raw key is shown once at creation and cannot be recovered</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>4</td><td>On failure</td><td>Invalid or inactive keys return <code>401 Unauthorized</code> with header <code>WWW-Authenticate: Basic realm="TAXII 2.1"</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>5</td><td>Rate limiting</td><td>120 requests per 60-second sliding window per key. Exceeding returns <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with <code>Retry-After</code> header</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-code-block">
                    <div class="taxii-code-title">Example: cURL Authentication</div>
                    <pre><code># Discovery
curl -u "taxii:YOUR_API_KEY" https://declawed.io/.well-known/taxii2

# List collections
curl -u "taxii:YOUR_API_KEY" https://declawed.io/taxii2/collections/

# Fetch objects from exposed-infrastructure
curl -u "taxii:YOUR_API_KEY" \
  "https://declawed.io/taxii2/collections/6b4f6112-e0af-5390-9e86-0d61ff9129f6/objects/?limit=50"</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="research-section">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div class="section-icon strike-icon"><img src="/assets/strike_icon.png" alt="STRIKE" /></div>
                    <h2>Pagination</h2>
                    <span class="section-badge">CURSOR-BASED</span>
                </div>
                <div class="section-explainer">
                    <h4>Efficient Data Retrieval</h4>
                    <p>The objects endpoint supports cursor-based pagination for efficient traversal of large result sets.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-tw">
                    <table class="taxii-t">
                        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>integer</td><td>100</td><td>Number of database rows to fetch (1&ndash;1000). Each row may produce multiple STIX objects.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>added_after</code></td><td>ISO 8601</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Only return objects added after this timestamp</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>next</code></td><td>string</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Opaque cursor from previous response for next page</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>match[type]</code></td><td>string</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Filter by STIX object type (e.g., <code>infrastructure</code>, <code>vulnerability</code>)</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-code-block">
                    <div class="taxii-code-title">Pagination Response Structure</div>
                    <pre><code>{
  "objects": [ ... ],
  "more": true,
  "next": "eyJvZmZzZXQiOiAxMDAsICJ0cyI6ICIyMDI2LTAxLTE1VDEyOjAwOjAwLjAwMFoifQ=="
}</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="research-section">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div class="section-icon strike-icon"><img src="/assets/strike_icon.png" alt="STRIKE" /></div>
                    <h2>Caching & Rate Limits</h2>
                    <span class="section-badge">PERFORMANCE</span>
                </div>
                <div class="section-explainer">
                    <h4>Fair Use Policy</h4>
                    <p>Rate limits are enforced per API key using a sliding window. Exceeding the limit returns <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with a <code>Retry-After</code> header indicating when to retry.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-tw">
                    <table class="taxii-t">
                        <thead><tr><th>Policy</th><th>Value</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>Rate Limit</td><td><strong>120 requests / 60 seconds</strong></td><td>Per API key, sliding window, applies to all TAXII endpoints</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Exceeded Response</td><td><code>429 Too Many Requests</code></td><td>Includes <code>Retry-After</code> header (seconds until window resets)</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Cache TTL (Objects)</td><td>120 seconds</td><td>Server-side cache reduces database load on repeated queries</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Cache TTL (Single Object)</td><td>300 seconds</td><td>Individual object lookups cached longer</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- INTEGRATION EXAMPLES -->
            <div class="section-group-header"><h3><span>Integration Examples</span></h3></div>

            <section class="research-section">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div class="section-icon strike-icon"><img src="/assets/strike_icon.png" alt="STRIKE" /></div>
                    <h2>Quick Start</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="section-explainer">
                    <h4>Common Integration Patterns</h4>
                    <p>DECLAWED TAXII feeds are compatible with any TAXII 2.1 client. Below are examples for common platforms and tools.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-code-block">
                    <div class="taxii-code-title">Python (taxii2-client)</div>
                    <pre><code>from taxii2client.v21 import Server

server = Server(
    "https://declawed.io/.well-known/taxii2",
    user="taxii",
    password="YOUR_API_KEY"
)

api_root = server.api_roots[0]
for collection in api_root.collections:
    print(f"{collection.title} ({collection.id})")
    bundle = collection.get_objects(limit=10)
    for obj in bundle.get("objects", []):
        print(f"  {obj['type']}: {obj.get('name', obj['id'])}")</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-code-block">
                    <div class="taxii-code-title">OpenCTI Connector</div>
                    <pre><code># docker-compose.yml addition for OpenCTI
opencti-connector-taxii:
  image: opencti/connector-taxii2:latest
  environment:
    - TAXII2_DISCOVERY_URL=https://declawed.io/.well-known/taxii2
    - TAXII2_USERNAME=taxii
    - TAXII2_PASSWORD=YOUR_API_KEY
    - TAXII2_COLLECTIONS=*
    - TAXII2_INTERVAL=3600</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div class="taxii-code-block">
                    <div class="taxii-code-title">MISP Feed Integration</div>
                    <pre><code># In MISP: Sync Actions &rarr; List Feeds &rarr; Add Feed
# URL: https://declawed.io/taxii2/collections/{collection_id}/objects/
# Authentication: Basic Auth
# Username: taxii
# Password: YOUR_API_KEY
# Input Source: TAXII 2.1</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

